-- title:
--   Capitulation kills p-primary classes dying in the idèles
-- statement:
--   Let $E \subseteq K \subseteq K''$ be number fields (with the scalar tower $E \to K \to K''$), with $K/E$ and $K''/E$ Galois, and let $S$ be a finite set of height-one primes of $\mathcal{O}_E$. Suppose given Galois descent data $D$ for the adèle ring of $K$, i.e. a monoid homomorphism $\mathrm{Gal}(K/E) \to \mathrm{RingAut}(\mathbf{A}_K)$ by continuous ring automorphisms extending the action on $K$, together with a multiplicative action of $\mathrm{Gal}(K/E)$ on $\mathbf{A}_K^\times$ which by `hactI` is the one induced by $D$; and likewise $D''$ and `hactI''` for $K''$. Let $M$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-representation of $\mathrm{Gal}(K/E)$ with an equivariant map $\iota$ to the additive group of $\mathbf{A}_K^\times$ which is injective and whose image is exactly the subgroup generated by the principal idèles (the image of $K^\times$) together with those idèles whose finite component at each prime not lying under a member of $S$ is a unit of the local integers, as is its inverse; let $M''$, $\iota''$ satisfy the same conditions over $K''$. Let $B : \mathrm{Res}\,M \to M''$ be a map of representations of $\mathrm{Gal}(K''/E)$ along restriction of automorphisms, compatible via $\iota, \iota''$ with the unit map of the ring homomorphism $\beta : \mathbf{A}_K \to \mathbf{A}_{K''}$ of the genuine adèle base change. Let $p$ be a prime and assume capitulation: every ideal $I$ of $\mathcal{O}_K$ with $I^{p^k}$ principal and nonzero, for some $k$, becomes principal in $\mathcal{O}_{K''}$. Then for $u \in H^2(\mathrm{Gal}(K/E), M)$ killed by $p^k$ and mapping to $0$ in $H^2(\mathrm{Gal}(K/E), \mathbf{A}_K^\times)$ under $\iota$, the image of $u$ in $H^2(\mathrm{Gal}(K''/E), M'')$ under restriction and $B$ vanishes.
--
--   This is the cohomological form of the statement that capitulation of the $p$-part of the $S$-class group of $K$ in $K''$ annihilates, after base change, those $p$-primary classes in $H^2(\mathrm{Gal}(K/E), K^\times J_K^S)$ that die in the idèles; the quotient of the idèles by $K^\times J_K^S$ is the $S$-class group, which is finite, and the connecting map of the corresponding short exact sequence carries the argument. It is used in the construction of $S$-unit cocycle lifts, via [`NumberField.IdeleLocalInv.exists_cocyclesTwo_sUnitsRep_map_toUnitsRep_eq_of_capitulation`](thm.html#NumberField.IdeleLocalInv.exists_cocyclesTwo_sUnitsRep_map_toUnitsRep_eq_of_capitulation).
